Create Docker Image from Running Container (official:xfusion)
This guide outlines the steps performed to create a new Docker image from a running container on Application Server 2 (stapp02) as requested by the Nautilus development team.

Task Overview
Server: Application Server 2 (stapp02)

Source Container: ubuntu_latest

Target Image Name & Tag: official:xfusion

Step-by-Step Procedure
1. Connect to Application Server 2
From the jump host, log in to Application Server 2 using SSH:

Bash
ssh steve@stapp02
(Password: Am3ric@)

2. Commit Container Changes to a New Image
Create the backup image from the running container using the docker commit command:

Bash
docker commit ubuntu_latest official:xfusion
3. Verify the Image Creation
Confirm that the image was successfully generated and registered locally:

Bash
docker images | grep official
